---
// "CIPLE, DEPLE or Celpe-Bras?": which exam fits which purpose (content-plan §2). General orientation,
// every fact "to verify". Text lives in public/i18n/en.json; the markup holds the same English as a fallback.
// No Celpe-Bras practice set: described only. Report: reports/exams-compare.md.
import ExamDisclaimer from "../../components/ExamDisclaimer.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import "../../styles/practice.css";
import "../../styles/pruefungen.css";

const purposes = [
  { key: "nationality", title: "Residence and nationality in Portugal", answer: "CIPLE (A2)", text: "For the language proof in a residence or nationality application, the usual exam is the CIPLE, level A2 of the CAPLE certificates, taken at an exam centre approved by CAPLE (University of Lisbon). Some people are exempt, and other proofs, such as a school certificate, can count in some procedures. The rules and the accepted levels changed in 2024–2025, so ask the office that handles your case (AIMA, the Conservatória dos Registos Centrais) before you book. To verify." },
  { key: "work", title: "Work", answer: "Depends on the employer", text: "Employers in Portugal usually care about your level more than the name of the exam. A CIPLE or DEPLE certificate is a clear, recognised proof. Regulated professions and public jobs can set a level, such as B1 or B2, so read the call for applications. A Brazilian employer or a company working with Brazil may know the Celpe-Bras better. To verify for your case." },
  { key: "university", title: "University and study", answer: "Ask the institution", text: "Portuguese universities that need proof of Portuguese often ask for B1 or B2, which points to the DEPLE or DIPLE. Some run their own Portuguese courses and tests instead. Brazilian universities and programmes for foreign students often ask for the Celpe-Bras. Each institution sets its own rule, so get it in writing. To verify." },
  { key: "brazil", title: "Brazil or Portugal?", answer: "Pick the country you will live in", text: "The two exams are built for two varieties. The CAPLE exams are written for European Portuguese and are the ones the Portuguese authorities know. The Celpe-Bras is Brazil's exam and is set around Brazilian usage. A certificate from one country is not automatically accepted in the other. Check with the office that will read your result. To verify." },
  { key: "self", title: "For yourself", answer: "Your choice", text: "If you want a goal at a level you choose, the CAPLE exams give you one certificate per level, from A1 to C2. The Celpe-Bras does not work like that: you take one exam, and the result is a level of the Brazilian scale, if you reach one." },
];

const rows = [
  { key: "who", label: "Who is behind it", caple: "CAPLE, the assessment centre at the University of Lisbon, with approved centres in Portugal and abroad", celpe: "Inep (Brazil's Ministry of Education) with the Brazilian foreign ministry, at accredited centres in Brazil and abroad" },
  { key: "levels", label: "Levels", caple: "ACESSO A1, CIPLE A2, DEPLE B1, DIPLE B2, DAPLE C1, DUPLE C2", celpe: "Four profiles: Intermediário, Intermediário Superior, Avançado, Avançado Superior. No A1 to C2 labels" },
  { key: "shape", label: "One exam or several", caple: "A separate exam for each level: you choose your level when you register", celpe: "One exam for everybody: the result says which level you reached, if any" },
  { key: "result", label: "Result", caple: "Pass or fail for the level you chose. Pass marks to verify", celpe: "A certificate with the level reached, or no certificate. Scoring to verify" },
  { key: "doc", label: "What you get", caple: "A certificate for that level", celpe: "A certificate with the level, issued by the Brazilian authorities" },
  { key: "valid", label: "How long it lasts", caple: "No expiry date as far as known. To verify", celpe: "No expiry date as far as known. To verify" },
  { key: "how", label: "How you take it", caple: "Papers on reading, writing, listening and speaking at an exam centre. Details to verify", celpe: "A written part that mixes reading, listening and writing in tasks, and a speaking interview. Details to verify" },
  { key: "when", label: "When", caple: "On fixed dates in the year, with a registration deadline. Dates to verify", celpe: "Usually once or twice a year, on dates set by Inep. Dates to verify" },
  { key: "fast", label: "How fast the result comes", caple: "To verify with your centre", celpe: "To verify with your centre or Inep" },
  { key: "price", label: "Price, roughly", caple: "Set by each centre. To verify", celpe: "Set by Inep and the centre. To verify" },
];
---
<Layout
  title="CIPLE, DEPLE or Celpe-Bras? Which Portuguese exam you need – icanspeak Portuguese"
  description="CIPLE, DEPLE or Celpe-Bras: which Portuguese exam fits residence, nationality, work or study, in Portugal or Brazil? Side by side, general orientation, to verify."
>
  <SiteNav active="pruefungen" />
  <main class="practice-main practice-main--wide">
    <a href="/exams" class="vp-back-link" data-i18n="fallen.back">Back to the exams</a>

    <div class="practice-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="delesiele.eyebrow">Choosing an exam</p>
      <h1 data-i18n="delesiele.title">CIPLE, DEPLE or Celpe-Bras?</h1>
      <p data-i18n="delesiele.lead">These are the main certificates of Portuguese as a foreign language. The CAPLE exams (CIPLE, DEPLE and the others) belong to Portugal, and the Celpe-Bras belongs to Brazil. What decides between them is what you need the result for. For residence and nationality in Portugal the usual answer is the CIPLE.</p>
      <ExamDisclaimer />
    </div>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.purpose.title">What do you need it for?</h2>
      {/* Headed paragraphs, not a table: these answers are too long for narrow columns on a phone. */}
      {purposes.map((p) => (
        <>
          <h3 data-i18n={`delesiele.p.${p.key}.title`}>{p.title}</h3>
          <p><strong data-i18n={`delesiele.p.${p.key}.answer`}>{p.answer}</strong></p>
          <p data-i18n={`delesiele.p.${p.key}.text`}>{p.text}</p>
          {p.key === "nationality" && <p><a href="/nationality" data-i18n="nat.link.more">How nationality by residence works, step by step</a></p>}
        </>
      ))}
      <p class="format-note" data-i18n="delesiele.purpose.note">General orientation, not legal advice. Rules change, so before you pay for an exam, check with the office that will read your result.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.compare.title">The exams side by side</h2>
      <div class="format-table-wrap">
        <table class="format-table">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th translate="no">CAPLE (CIPLE, DEPLE …)</th><th translate="no">Celpe-Bras</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-i18n={`delesiele.r.${r.key}.label`}>{r.label}</th>
                <td data-i18n={`delesiele.r.${r.key}.caple`}>{r.caple}</td>
                <td data-i18n={`delesiele.r.${r.key}.celpe`}>{r.celpe}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="format-note" data-i18n="delesiele.compare.note">Every fact in this table is general orientation and is marked &quot;to verify&quot; until it is checked against the official sites: formats, dates, prices and recognition change. Check the current rules of CAPLE and Celpe-Bras before you book.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.tips.title">If you still can't decide</h2>
      <ul class="task-points">
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.1">You live in Portugal and need a proof for AIMA or nationality: the CIPLE is the usual answer. Check the level your procedure asks for.</li>
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.2">You are not sure of your level: take the placement test here first, then pick the CAPLE exam for the level you reach.</li>
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.3">You plan to study or work in Brazil: the Celpe-Bras is the exam to ask about. Practise Brazilian vocabulary and accents too.</li>
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.4">You learn European Portuguese only: aim for the CAPLE exams. This course practises for them, not for the Celpe-Bras.</li>
        <li data-i18n="delesiele.tips.5">You want a certificate that does not expire: both seem to have none, but verify this in the current rules.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.practice.title">Practise here</h2>
      <div class="mock-cta">
        <h3 data-i18n="delesiele.practice.caple.title">CAPLE exams</h3>
        <p data-i18n="delesiele.practice.caple.text">Format and practice tests for ACESSO A1, CIPLE A2, DEPLE B1, DIPLE B2 and DAPLE C1, in the style of the exams.</p>
        <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/dele" data-i18n="delesiele.practice.caple.cta">To the CAPLE page</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mock-cta">
        <h3 data-i18n="delesiele.practice.celpe.title">Celpe-Bras</h3>
        <p data-i18n="delesiele.practice.celpe.text">We describe the Celpe-Bras here, but we have no practice set for it. Our practice material is for the CAPLE exams.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="exam-section">
      <h2 data-i18n="delesiele.sources.title">Where to check</h2>
      <ul class="task-points">
        <li><a href="https://caple.letras.ulisboa.pt" rel="noopener" data-i18n="delesiele.sources.caple">CAPLE: Portuguese as a foreign language exams</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.gov.br/inep/pt-br/areas-de-atuacao/avaliacao-e-exames-educacionais/celpe-bras" rel="noopener" data-i18n="delesiele.sources.celpe">Celpe-Bras: information from Inep</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
